int Republican baseline gives Spartz a clear structural edge, though the 2026 national climate has shifted toward Democrats, and reporting notes national Democrats have added the seat to their target list.\n\nThe only public poll, a Democratic-sponsored survey from July, showed Spartz ahead just 48-46, and Ford has raised a credible sum. Still, expert raters uniformly place the race in the Likely or Safe Republican column, and prediction markets give Ford roughly a one-in-six chance. Spartz's modest cash position is the main soft spot. The forecast calls for a Republican hold in the mid-single digits, short of safe territory given the environment and thin polling.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0883, "margin": -8.48}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1386, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.1079, "margin": -9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1359, "margin": -8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1346, "margin": -7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.1196, "margin": -7.5}]}